From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qa <qa@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:29:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] LICENSE: drop the note that named Waydroid as a
 dependency

The MIT text is untouched. Below it stood an informational note: "This
project drives the Waydroid program (GPL-3.0) as an installed dependency
through its public command-line interface." After the removal of the
Waydroid backend that sentence is false, so the note now says that the
project has no Android runtime dependency.

Kept as a commit of its own because it edits the licence file, and the
project owner has not explicitly approved a change there. Dropping this
commit leaves everything else working; only
tests/test_no_waydroid.py::test_the_licence_file_does_not_name_waydroid_as_a_dependency
and the test totals in README/TESTING/ROADMAP go with it.

pytest: 1061 passed, 1 skipped (1062 collected).

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
